db/ref 1079 #uuid "d084d670-2e7b-5600-a90e-83f0ea45658b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554522 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d9447dc2-1b9f-505d-ae0d-6cd7412e4910" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554526 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e8f2f208-bfdf-5d7a-b0b7-7f94fe8a16ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554560 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554560 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554560 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554560 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d4/d4573a2e3c7b220ac363c996c5332a3db93cc48b5b941e46a529b6912804f0c6.png)\n\nThe triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over the region $R$ (shown above) can be expressed as the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y-z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nRewrite this repeated integral by integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $y,$ and then $z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554560 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31b80dba-d43f-591d-b1ec-e6cb3d1597c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554560 #edb/ref 1074 "From the given repeated integral, we see that $R$ can be written as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{y}^{2},\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-y-z\\}\n$$\n\nWe wish to rewrite our triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nSince both repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $x,$ the $x$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y-z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/8d/8d1db6e886f00596814900ca0c4113590a37a407b65c800eb1f9926328ade50c.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type I region in the $yz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{y}^{2}\\}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y$ to $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z,$ we write $D$ as a type II region.\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(z),$ is \n\n$$\nz=1-{y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt{1-z}.\n$$\n\nand the left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nThen, the type II representation of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-z}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/1f/1fe8a810a7e98c8a40739d5019ff9054a5375c0a12ae7fd1b17f8b6c8bb19f75.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y-z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554589 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554589 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554589 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554589 #edb/ref 1071 "By changing the order of integration in the following repeated integrals so that they are integrated first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y,$ express the following sum as a single repeated integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2z}{\\int }_{-y}^{z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-z}{\\int }_{-y}^{z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554589 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7da71e9d-63e8-5f19-957f-ca4c328a0eb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554589 #edb/ref 1074 "We wish to find the limits of integration such that our integral can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integrals, we see that the domain of integration $R={R}_{1}\\cup {R}_{2},$ where ${R}_{1}$ and ${R}_{2}$ are type II regions, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2z,\\,\\,-y\\le x\\le z\\}, \\\\ {R}_{2} & =\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-z,\\,\\,-y\\le x\\le z\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince all repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $x,$ the $x$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{-y}^{z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/9b/9b8806738b61c4ce692f555261abcd9918096a7585291954a7f11c39aadeab39.png)\n\nThe region $D$ consists of two type II regions in the $yz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2z\\}\\,\\cup \\,\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-z\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the bottom boundary of the region, written in the form $z=z(y),$ is\n\n$$\ny=2z\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{y}{2}\n$$\n\nand the top boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=3-z\\,⟹\\,z=3-y.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le z\\le 3-y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d1/d1a9d83672ffbd372b6a994c62771291d957e6a5c13189a6baea6d544f6a1bbc.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3-y}{\\int }_{-y}^{z}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554615 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554615 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162495" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554615 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554615 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2f/2f95783c1e9624e58b4cd26764e94fb61d45c7aa75260ce8ca726a6c2e5db9ab.png)\n\nThe triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over the region $R$ (shown above) can be expressed as the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3-3z/2}^{3}{\\int }_{8-4x/3-2z}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nRewrite this repeated integral by integrating first with respect to $y,$ then $z,$ and then $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ac81bb63-6896-5260-96a8-5a88cb11f40d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554615 #edb/ref 1074 "From the given repeated integral, we see that $R$ can be written as a type III region as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,3-\\frac{3z}{2}\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,8-\\frac{4x}{3}-2z\\le y\\le 4\\}\n$$\n\nWe wish to rewrite our triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nSince both repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $y,$ the $y$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{8-4x/3-2z}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/85/85d184f328ebdbed5faf2d1c43261940a8241b6637450ab5fe1c8d803026e273.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type II region in the $xz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,3-\\frac{3z}{2}\\le x\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the bottom  boundary of the region, written in the form $z=z(x),$ is \n\n$$\nx=3-\\frac{3z}{2}\\,⟹\\,z=2-\\frac{2x}{3}\n$$\n\nand the top boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nz=2.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,2-\\frac{2x}{3}\\le z\\le 2\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/6a/6ac58e4c98c79a1a698d052479b55a45dd2b79bed4ca11422d172fe306dac15f.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{2-2x/3}^{2}{\\int }_{8-4/3x-2z}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554640 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554640 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162326" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554640 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554640 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\n*Hint: First change the order of integration to $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554640 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f35d7c5d-0e2d-5ee0-b1c5-16c26213b1d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554640 #edb/ref 1074 "We wish to find the limits of integration such that our integral can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the domain of integration $R$ can be written as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\le z\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\}\n$$\n\nSince all repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $x,$ the $x$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/ed/ed7308cf6c77f5d89b94ec90237fa9161fc85429182813f38b55d916bdbdaeef.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is type I region in the $yz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\le z\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y$ to $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z,$ we write $D$ as a type II region.\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\ny=0\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region $D,$ written in the form $y=y(z),$ is\n\n$$\nz=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\,⟹\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡z.\n$$\n\nThen, the type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/4f/4fb3323b2c295df8351910890f20266840b131a4dfd8a7bba0d61a3eb03bea23.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}[\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,[x]_{0}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,[y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{3}{(1+{cos}^{2}⁡z)}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[(1+0)^{3/2}-(1+1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(1-{2}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554646 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554646 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554646 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554646 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8f/8fc551f1439ed5a551ae8fd18234479bb062d43ae9e4faf55d896739f76e0f4d.png)\n\nThe triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over the region $R$ (shown above) can be expressed as the following repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{4/z}{\\int }_{0}^{4-yz}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nRewrite this repeated integral by integrating first with respect to $x,$ then $z,$ and then $y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554646 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fff4e417-ea88-59e6-bd63-239378f4d2c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554646 #edb/ref 1074 "From the given repeated integral, we see that $R$ can be written as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le 4,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le \\frac{4}{z},\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-yz\\}\n$$\n\nWe wish to rewrite our triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nSince both repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $x,$ the $x$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{0}^{4-yz}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/9a/9a59198b60398e2b3044296c3cc76b4748785303029dccc1087320cd11cb7d55.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type II region in the $yz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le 4,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le \\frac{4}{z}\\}\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $z=z(y),$ is \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{4}{z}\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{4}{y}\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nz=1.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\,1\\le z\\le \\frac{4}{y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/9b/9bc88aa4f0ad07d89ff5dd3c0de16208cb8bf47d774b557a7bf2140790c95291.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{4/y}{\\int }_{0}^{4-yz}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
